$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
2,5-disubstituted furans 4a-z. To a flame-dried schlenk tube were added
phosphorane 1 (0.25 mmol, 1.0 eq) and glyoxal derivatives 2 (0.3 mmol,
1.2 eq). The tube was vacuumized and back-filled with N2, followed by the
addition of 1.0 mL of anhydrous ClCH2CH2Cl. The resulting mixture was
stirred at 80 °C for 1 hour. After cooling to room temperature, HSiCl3
(58 mg, 45 uL, 0.5 mmol) was added in one portion and the reaction
mixture was stirred vigorously. After full conversion of the intermediate
enone IV by TLC analysis, two drops of MeOH was added into the resulting
mixture and further vigorously stirring was needed to promote the
transformation of the intermediate 1,4-diketone V to the furan product.
Then the solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the residue was
directly subjected to flash column chromatograph using petroleum
ether/ethyl acetate as the eluent. The desired 2,5-disubstitued furans
4a-z. Column chromatography gave product 4d 6 in 71% yield (45.1 mg) as
white solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.72-7.70 (m, 2H), 7.65-7.62 (m,
2H), 7.41-7.32 (m, 4H), 7.28-7.22 (m, 1H), 6.71-6.68 (m, 2H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 153.56, 152.15, 132.82, 130.47, 129.16, 128.85,
128.69, 127.47, 124.81, 123.69, 107.65, 107.25.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-waste reduction, one-pot Wittig/1,4-reduction/Paal-Knorr
sequence, Ph3PO generated in stage 1 and HCl generated in stage 3 acting
as catalysts, screw capped pressure tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Successively Recycle Waste as Catalyst: A One-Pot
Wittig/1,4-Reduction/Paal-Knorr Sequence for Modular Synthesis of
Substituted Furans
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Long; Du, Yi; Zeng, Xing-Ping; Shi, Tao-Da; Zhou, Feng; Zhou, Jian
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(6), 1557-1560

