$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the synthesis of
trisubstituted furans 5aa-ah. To a flame-dried schlenk tube were added
α-methyl substituted phosphorane 1o (0.25 mmol, 1.0 equiv) and glyoxal
derivatives 2 (0.3 mmol, 1.2 equivs). The tube was vacuumized and
back-filled with N2, followed by adding 1.0 mL of anhydrous ClCH2CH2Cl.
The resulting mixture was stirred at 80 oC for 1 hour. After cooling
down, HSiCl3 (58 mg, 45 uL, 0.5 mmol) was added in one portion and the
reaction mixture was stirred vigorously. After full conversion of the
intermediate VI by TLC analysis, two drops of MeOH was added into the
resulting mixture and further vigorously stirring was needed to promote
the transformation of the intermediate 1,4-diketones VII to the furan
product. Then the solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the
residue was directly subjected to flash column chromatograph using
petroleum ether/ethyl acetate as the eluent. The desired trisubstituted
furans 5aa-ah. Column chromatography afforded the desired product 5af in
70% yield (49.7 mg) as white solid. Mp 111-113 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 8.19 (s, 1H), 7.90-7.77 (m, 6H), 7.52-7.43 (m, 4H), 7.33-7.29
(m, 1H), 6.75 (s, 1H), 2.37 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 151.68,
148.46, 133.57, 132.58, 131.69, 128.58, 128.32, 128.10, 128.03, 127.74,
126.73, 126.44, 125.78, 125.25, 122.23, 121.80, 118.83, 111.50, 12.17; IR
(neat): 2971, 1625, 1490, 1015, 835, 747, 686 cm-1; GC-MS (EI): 284 (M+,
100), 129 (39), 77 (32), 241 (30), 179 (24), 105 (15); HRMS (EI): Exact
mass calcd for C21H16O: 284.1201, Found: 284.1203.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-waste reduction, one-pot Wittig/1,4-reduction/Paal-Knorr
sequence, Ph3PO generated in stage 1 and HCl generated in stage 3 acting
as catalysts, screw capped pressure tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Successively Recycle Waste as Catalyst: A One-Pot
Wittig/1,4-Reduction/Paal-Knorr Sequence for Modular Synthesis of
Substituted Furans
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Chen, Long; Du, Yi; Zeng, Xing-Ping; Shi, Tao-Da; Zhou, Feng; Zhou, Jian
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(6), 1557-1560

